{"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"text":" — a controllable ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" conformer for previews and tests that does not touch ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockServiceReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPreviewAndTest","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/ServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/ServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/UIComponentsReference"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"current"}]},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement snapshot the way the real service reflects RevenueCat’s state: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" updates it and pushes it through the stream, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo()"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"text":" return it. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/finish()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" tears the stream down, and the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/customerInfoError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/restoreError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" properties inject failures for testing error paths.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This mock differs from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" in SwiduxPaywall: that mock’s stream finishes after the initial yield, which is fine for static previews but cannot model purchase, refund, or family-share updates as a sequence. This mock keeps the stream live until you tear it down."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For preview and test patterns built on this type, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPreviewAndTest","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Library-target","text":"Library target","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Types","text":"Types","type":"heading","level":2},{"anchor":"docSwiduxRevenueCatPaywalldocumentationSwiduxRevenueCatPaywallMockRevenueCatPaywallService","text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService``","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public final class MockRevenueCatPaywallService: PaywallService, @unchecked Sendable {","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","","    public var customerInfoError: Error?","    public var restoreError: Error?","","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","","    public func send(_ snapshot: EntitlementSnapshot)","    public func finish()","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference type. Internal state is guarded by an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLock"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@unchecked Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" because the protected mutable state lives behind that lock."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Initializer","text":"Initializer","type":"heading","level":4},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro"},{"type":"text","text":" — Initial value for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot.isPro"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"},{"type":"text","text":" — Initial value for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot.hasPermanentLicense"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The values supplied here become the starting "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"current"}]},{"type":"text","text":" snapshot — what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo()"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":" return and what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoStream()"},{"type":"text","text":" yields first, until "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" replaces it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"customerInfoError--restoreError","text":"`customerInfoError` \/ `restoreError`","type":"heading","level":4},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional errors thrown by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":" respectively while set ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", the default, means success). Set them to drive the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed"},{"type":"text","text":" path, retry affordances, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":"’s last-known-good fallback; clear them to restore success."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"customerInfo-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","text":"`customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","type":"heading","level":4},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the current snapshot — the init-time state, or the latest value passed to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". This matches the real service: the plugin’s dismiss-triggered refresh sees the same state the stream delivered, so a simulated purchase does not regress to free on refresh. Throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/customerInfoError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead when it is set."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"customerInfoStream-%3E-AsyncStream%3CEntitlementSnapshot%3E","text":"`customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>`","type":"heading","level":4},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yields the current snapshot, then every value passed to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The stream stays open until "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/finish()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call to this method replaces the active continuation and finishes the previous stream, so an earlier subscriber’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop terminates instead of hanging. Only the most recent subscriber receives subsequent "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" updates."}]}]},{"anchor":"restorePurchases-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","text":"`restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","type":"heading","level":4},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the current snapshot, exactly like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo()"},{"type":"text","text":". Throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/restoreError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead when it is set."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"docSwiduxRevenueCatPaywalldocumentationSwiduxRevenueCatPaywallMockRevenueCatPaywallServicesend","text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)``","type":"heading","level":4},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public func send(_ snapshot: EntitlementSnapshot)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes the snapshot current and pushes it to the active stream subscriber. If no stream is active, the snapshot is still recorded — only the stream delivery is skipped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this to simulate purchase, expiration, or family-share updates during a test."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"docSwiduxRevenueCatPaywalldocumentationSwiduxRevenueCatPaywallMockRevenueCatPaywallServicefinish","text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/finish()``","type":"heading","level":4},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public func finish()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Finishes the active entitlement stream. Iterators terminate cleanly. Subsequent calls to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService\/send(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" still update the current snapshot but are no longer delivered to a stream."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call this in test teardown or when a preview is done observing entitlement transitions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Lifecycle-example","text":"Lifecycle example","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let mock = MockRevenueCatPaywallService(isPro: false)","let stream = mock.customerInfoStream()","","var iterator = stream.makeAsyncIterator()","let initial = await iterator.next()  \/\/ EntitlementSnapshot(isPro: false, ...)","","mock.send(EntitlementSnapshot(isPro: true))","let updated = await iterator.next()  \/\/ EntitlementSnapshot(isPro: true, ...)","","mock.finish()","let terminal = await iterator.next()  \/\/ nil — stream finished","","let refreshed = try await mock.customerInfo()  \/\/ EntitlementSnapshot(isPro: true, ...) — send(_:) updated it"]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/mockservicereference"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"role":"article","title":"Mock Service Reference"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/MockRevenueCatPaywallService":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" conformer for previews and tests with a controllable entitlement stream.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockRevenueCatPaywallService","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/mockrevenuecatpaywallservice","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/HowToPreviewAndTest":{"title":"How to Preview and Test","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/howtopreviewandtest","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToPreviewAndTest","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Drive entitlement state from SwiftUI previews and tests with ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — no RevenueCat SDK call required.","type"